{:category :provenance, :timings {:predicted_ms 20711.031, :cache_n 72794, :predicted_per_second 86.71707362129872, :predicted_n 1796, :prompt_per_token_ms 0.9413718689788054, :prompt_ms 488.572, :prompt_n 519, :prompt_per_second 1062.2794593222698, :predicted_per_token_ms 11.531754454342984}, :finish-reason "stop", :reasoning "We need to answer: \"When did Sid first name the terminal purpose (humans living healthy forever), and in whose words is it recorded?\" Using only provided material. Must cite file and section.\n\nWe need to locate where Sid first named the terminal purpose \"humans living healthy forever\". Look through provided files.\n\nWe have several files: CLAUDE.md, docs/_map.md, docs/current-mental-model/BETS.md, docs/current-mental-model/build/relation-kernel/CONTRACT.md, docs/current-mental-model/build/trail-view/CONTRACT.md, docs/current-mental-model/build/trail-view/RETRO.md, docs/current-mental-model/build/trail-view/CONTRACT.md includes mention of \"North — Sid's commitment\". In BETS.md there is a section \"North — Sid's commitment\". It says: \"Softland is a land made of software — a place you inhabit, not a tool you use. A world for holding understanding in public form: trails that don't fade, a map that doesn't lie, one land at every zoom from the knowledge landscape down to the code that renders it — visitable by other minds, human and machine, and renovatable by its inhabitants down to bedrock. It should exist even if the route is long: first the wall made alive, then a settlement, then a world.\n\n**The question the land exists to answer, about any xyz:** what are the known knowns, the known unknowns — and where do the unknown unknowns announce themselves? Rendered as a knowledge earth: zoomed out, topics are nations with visible borders and connections; zoomed all the way in, the ground is made of questions, claims, evidence, sources. Every zoom level is a level of understanding, with AI holding the context of that level — and every visitor arrives with their own assistant, tuned to how *they* understand. Symbiotic, not AI-dependent: machines carry the boring weight; humans at every level of understanding explore and contribute at theirs. The substrate already speaks this question's grammar: claims-with-evidence are the known knowns; first-class questions are the known unknowns; the frontier — where trails end, evidence thins, and dense nations have no roads between them — is where unknown unknowns announce themselves. (The map renders the shoreline of ignorance, not the contents of the dark.)\n\n**Not one person's tool:** a vibrant ecosystem of humans and agents on different layers — Rama the scalable ground truth, Electric the reactive tissue, WebGPU the visible world (one day 3D interactive models: drug structures, living systems, local minds running beside you), LLMs and humans in symbiosis. A social network for collective intelligence: the idea map for builders of what can now be built on top of science — and when they get to building, the paradigm is the same land, one layer down.\n\n**Why it must exist:** the map humanity has of what it knows is fragmented, hard to evaluate, and loses track of its own progress. Sid wants a reasonable attack on the outcome of **humans living healthy forever** — the map is the instrument; longevity is the first territory it must serve.\"\n\nThus the phrase \"humans living healthy forever\" appears in that paragraph. It says \"Sid wants a reasonable attack on the outcome of **humans living healthy forever**\". So that is the terminal purpose. The question: When did Sid first name the terminal purpose (humans living healthy forever), and in whose words is it recorded?\n\nIt appears in the same paragraph, but we need to locate the exact source: It appears in the \"North — Sid's commitment\" section of `docs/current-mental-model/BETS.md`. Also appears in `vision/LOG.md` maybe. Let's search: In BETS.md we have that paragraph. It says \"Sid wants a reasonable attack on the outcome of **humans living healthy forever** — the map is the instrument; longevity is the first territory it must serve.\"\n\nThus the answer: It appears in BETS.md, in the \"North — Sid's commitment\" section. The question asks \"When did Sid first name the terminal purpose (humans living healthy forever), and in whose words is it recorded?\" The answer: It was first named in the vision log? Actually the text appears in BETS.md as part of the description of North. It might also appear in vision/LOG.md earlier? Let's search within provided files: The snippet appears in BETS.md. Also appears in vision/LOG.md? In the Vision Log, there is a paragraph: \"Why it must exist: the map humanity has of what it knows is fragmented... Sid wants a reasonable attack on the outcome of **humans living healthy forever** — the map is the instrument; longevity is the first territory it must serve.\" That appears in the Vision Log as part of the description of North. Actually the Vision Log includes that text. Let's locate: In Vision Log, after describing the map, there is a paragraph: \"**Why it must exist:** the map humanity has of what it knows is fragmented, hard to evaluate, and loses track of its own progress. Sid wants a reasonable attack on the outcome of **humans living healthy forever** — the map is the instrument; longevity is the first territory it must serve.\"\n\nThus the phrase appears in Vision Log. The question: \"When did Sid first name the terminal purpose (humans living healthy forever), and in whose words is it recorded?\" The answer: It was first named in the Vision Log, specifically in the entry dated 2026-07-03? Actually the Vision Log entry is dated 2026-07-03? The Vision Log entry is part of the Vision Log file, which contains multiple entries. The relevant part is in the Vision Log entry that describes the terminal purpose. It appears in the Vision Log entry that begins \"Softland is a land made of software — a place you inhabit, not a tool you use..