ce kinds → A3 activity+R3 (relation-kernel amendments, gates 9/10/15/16) — gates 9, 10-kernel-half, 15, 16 green; suite 2 tests / 222 assertions / 0 failures; code + docs UNCOMMITTED (commits on Sid's word). Phase B (trail_view module + wrappers + text projection + fixtures; remaining gates 1–8, 11–14) IN FLIGHT this session (Opus subagent), then batched A1+A2+A3+B diff-falsification (fresh subagent), then Fable gate review.\"\n\nThus the relation-activity projection + R3 query is part of Phase A (relation kernel) work package. Specifically, it was produced during Phase A1 custody, A2 stance kinds, A3 activity+R3. The commit that landed it? In the retro, they mention \"code committed (`2796044`), docs trail committed (`736708f`+), retro run — `build/relation-kernel/RETRO.md`\". Also later \"git-spine WP2 + trail-room R-1 GATE-PASSED, FIXED, COMMITTED, CLOSED.\" But that's later.\n\nThe question: \"The relation-activity projection + R3 query: which WP phase produced it, and in which commit did it land?\" We need to answer based on provided material. The relevant file is `docs/current-mental-model/build/relation-kernel/RETRO.md` which mentions Phase A and the commit hash? It mentions \"code committed (`2796044`)\". That is a commit hash. It also mentions \"docs trail committed (`736708f`+)\". So the commit that introduced the relation-activity projection and R3 query likely is `2796044`. Let's verify: In the retro, they say \"code committed (`2796044`), docs trail committed (`736708f`+), retro run — `build/relation-kernel/RETRO.md`\". That suggests that commit 2796044 introduced the relation kernel module with the projection and R3 query.\n\nThus answer: It was produced in Phase A of the relation-kernel work package (the \"relation kernel\" WP). It landed in commit 2796044 (and also documented in 736708f). Provide citation: `docs/current-mental-model/build/relation-kernel/RETRO.md` section \"Package Retro — relation-kernel-module (closed 2026-07-03)\". Also maybe `doc